### W-194 — chat 152 (Cowork) — M's four rulings on DEF-143 item 11's open questions, and 26c-02 answered under ruling (c) by a hunt for the origin of each total, instrument r2-32a.py; BUILD184 -> BUILD185

- **The first chat since chat 143 whose subject is a ruling rather than a re-derivation.** DEF-143 item 11's order was emptied by chat 151-B's four segments (W-190 … W-193). What the order waited on was R3's rulings, and this chat put the four to M and took them. **M ruled: 26c-02 → (c) a third state, hunt the origin of each number; 27a-02 → (a) the column names entries that rest on the section; 28a-06 → (a) the figure is re-taken on the list it is printed beside; 28b-07 → (b) the block's lead-ins stop saying the chapters rest on it.** Only the first required work of this chat; the other three are seated as rulings for R3 to execute and are recorded in DEF-152.
- **§0 gate: GATE-ch152, verdict PASS**, run from a clean container against BUILD90 main + BUILD184 fetched from Drive by fileId. Both md5s asserted (`49065309b0c4fe8e055f693aed295cca`, `d4350094449e3a4bf488315e21199bd4`); 359 members extracted; the four governing members reproduced REBUILD-BUILD184's assertions exactly, which is also the proof this chat's extractor is byte-exact. census byte-identical; `run --core` 5/5; MANIFEST OK 358 listed / 359 extracted; **72 of 72 banked goldens OK on last value, non-OK zero**. §0a empty. **BUILD184 was in Drive as a whole file, so the five-step REBUILD chain was not needed** — a first since chat 149.
- **The open was corrected before any work was done.** Graphify's chat-151 → 152 handoff note (00:24 UTC) says chat 151 seated nothing and chat 152 opens on BUILD180 with 26b-02/-03 next. That was true when written and was superseded three hours later by chat 151-B's four closes. **A handoff note is a reading taken at a moment, exactly as §32.1.4.1 says of a figure about the book** — the same mechanism this chat then went on to measure in the volume. The GitHub probe the note made chat 152's first action was run once and 404'd again; the ruling is that the repository store-of-record is not executable from Cowork and no further session time goes to it (W-190's loop stands).
- **26c-02 IS ANSWERED, AND ITS OWN WORDING IS CORRECTED.** `r2-32a.py` (22,360 B, md5 `15a9047a`), golden `r2-32a.out` (16,587 B, md5 `0d5d75a2`, 179 lines), ALL INTEGRITY CHECKS OK with one deviation. **CONVENTION ORIG**, stated before scoring: a total's origin is the object that computed it, and a total is REPRODUCIBLE only if some assignment of values **printed somewhere in the six volumes or Prints & Proofs** to the four components §32.1.4's own table names sums to it; a value the record does not print may not be supplied to close an arithmetic. Fifth convention in five units, after FLOOR, DEP, AY and PROV.
- **55 is §32.1.4's own table and is the only one of the three a reader can reconstruct.** Four E-bearing rows — D unfibred 4, Q unfibred 1, the numbers 33, the audits 17 — sum to 55 exactly against L8978's word, and **(4, 1, 33, 17) is the only assignment of printed values that reaches 55.**
- **48 is register 373 / §32.1.4.1, and two of its four components are never restated.** The three-state table moves the numbers index 33 → 21 → 23 and E(Q) unfibred 1 → 1 → 4; Appendix D unfibred and the audit set are carried at their §32.1.4 values. 4 + 4 + 23 + 17 = 48 exactly. **Three printed assignments reach 48.**
- **47 does NOT enter the record at 375. It is register 332's, the entry §32.1.4 itself cites** — and the citation is invisible to a line-wise sweep because *Register* and *332.* sit on either side of a line break: line-wise [278, 285, 294], normalised join [278, 285, 294, **332**]. 332 states *THE TOTAL IS A READOUT THE PRESS PRINTS AT EVERY BUILD — 47 AT THE TIME OF WRITING, HAVING BEEN 55 WHEN THIS SECTION WAS FIRST COMPUTED.* **The total across the record is 55, 47, 48, 47 — not monotone. The record has it at 47 before it has it at 48, and 375 restates 332's figure rather than lowering 373's.** That is the mechanism behind 26c-02, and it is not the mechanism 26c-02 named.
- **32a-01 CORRECTS 26c-02 (the deviation).** 26c-02 recorded that the replacement *shape* sentence *appears in no volume*. Measured case-folded over all six volumes and Prints & Proofs, it has **two sites, both in the Register — entries 332 and 375**; zero in any chapter, zero in the other four compendia, zero in PP. What is true is narrower: **§32.1.4 does not carry it.** A claim about a volume is not a claim about a section. Recorded, not repaired.
